<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
  <!--
    The semantic icon catalog: one key per name a view may ask for, on a 24x24 grid.

    Every drawing here is a fallback. NutIconLibrary replaces all of these at start-up with geometry
    from Material Icons, so nothing in this file is what the user actually sees; it exists so a name
    still resolves to a glyph if a future version of the library stops carrying the kind mapped to
    it, and so the set of valid names is reviewable in one place. Adding a name here without also
    mapping it in NutIconLibrary is what the icon catalog tests fail on.

    PathIcon fills geometries and StreamGeometry uses the even-odd rule, so outlined glyphs are
    expressed as an outer subpath plus an inner subpath that punches the interior through.
    Keep new glyphs on the same grid and stroke weight (~1.6px equivalent) so scale stays uniform.
  -->

  <!-- Navigation -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="NutIconMenu">M3,5 L21,5 L21,7 L3,7 Z M3,11 L21,11 L21,13 L3,13 Z M3,17 L21,17 L21,19 L3,19 Z</StreamGeometry>
  <!-- Outlined house: one silhouette punched by its interior, so weight matches the other nav glyphs. -->
