  <StreamGeometry x:Key="NutIconSun">M12,7.4 A4.6,4.6 0 1 1 11.99,7.4 Z M12,9.1 A2.9,2.9 0 1 0 12.01,9.1 Z M11.1,1.4 L12.9,1.4 L12.9,5 L11.1,5 Z M11.1,19 L12.9,19 L12.9,22.6 L11.1,22.6 Z M1.4,11.1 L5,11.1 L5,12.9 L1.4,12.9 Z M19,11.1 L22.6,11.1 L22.6,12.9 L19,12.9 Z M4.2,5.5 L5.5,4.2 L8,6.7 L6.7,8 Z M16,17.3 L17.3,16 L19.8,18.5 L18.5,19.8 Z M18.5,4.2 L19.8,5.5 L17.3,8 L16,6.7 Z M5.5,19.8 L4.2,18.5 L6.7,16 L8,17.3 Z</StreamGeometry>
  <!--
    Crescent traced as one closed figure: the long way round the disc (centre 12,12 r=9) from one
    horn to the other, then back along the bite (centre 17.2,6.8 r=7.6). The endpoints are the real
    intersections of those two circles, so the horns close to a point rather than ending bluntly.

    A smaller bite pushed further out gives a full-bodied crescent with short horns. Keeping the
    bite nearly as large as the disc produces the opposite - a thin fingernail with long fragile
    horns that break up at 18px.

    The four craters are extra subpaths under the even-odd rule, so they are covered twice and come
    out as genuine holes: the surface behind shows through and they stay correct on any background,
    which a painted-on dot would not. Each sits clear of the disc edge, of the bite and of its
    neighbours, so no crater can break the silhouette or merge into another. Radii are 1.5, 1.1,
    1.0 and 0.85 - below about 0.8 they vanish into the antialiasing at this size.

    Subtracting one disc from another under the even-odd rule does not work for the bite itself:
    the part of the cutting disc falling outside the other is covered an odd number of times and
    fills in, turning the crescent into a ring. Only the fully enclosed craters can work this way.
  -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="NutIconMoon">F0 M10.55,3.12 A9,9 0 1 0 20.88,13.45 A7.6,7.6 0 0 1 10.55,3.12 Z M8,15.5 A1.5,1.5 0 1 0 11,15.5 A1.5,1.5 0 1 0 8,15.5 Z M11.5,19 A1,1 0 1 0 13.5,19 A1,1 0 1 0 11.5,19 Z M6.65,10.5 A0.85,0.85 0 1 0 8.35,10.5 A0.85,0.85 0 1 0 6.65,10.5 Z M14.2,17.4 A1.1,1.1 0 1 0 16.4,17.4 A1.1,1.1 0 1 0 14.2,17.4 Z</StreamGeometry>
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="NutIconProfile">M12,2.8 A4.8,4.8 0 1 1 11.99,2.8 Z M12,4.5 A3.1,3.1 0 1 0 12.01,4.5 Z M3.6,21.2 C3.6,16.4 7.4,13.6 12,13.6 C16.6,13.6 20.4,16.4 20.4,21.2 L18.7,21.2 C18.7,17.5 15.7,15.3 12,15.3 C8.3,15.3 5.3,17.5 5.3,21.2 Z</StreamGeometry>

